summary: platform/posix finds that the program's own input and output, which every lane gives /dev/null and captures, and a descriptor that is not open are no terminals, and that asking them a size or settings is ENOTTY; a pseudo-terminal it opens, both ends closed on exec, is a terminal whose size is set and read back, whose settings made raw pass a carriage return through unchanged and read back as they were set, and which, given back the settings it was found with, reads exactly those and turns a typed carriage return into a newline again
